        "id": 39651,
        "name": "Cosmonaut Zero",
        "username": "Cosmonaut_Zero",
        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/cosmonaut_zero/{size}/2520_2.png",
        "created_at": "2012-10-04T21:02:52.000Z",
        "cooked": "<p>I'm with TheJayMann here. There's a whole bunch of reasons why reading an implied \"is dealt damage\" in addition to \"deals damage\" makes no sense. For one, it breaks if there are damage increases or reductions that apply. Galvanize gives Fanatic +1 damage, so she actually takes 3 damage and the condition to not destroy it fails to trigger. Which is dumb. It also makes other cards which include an explicit \"if a target is dealt damage this way\" requirement redundant. If there's one thing I've learned about the templating in SotM, it's that economy of words is important to the team (eg: every instance of \"would\" that lacks an \"instead\").</p><p>Consistently throughout the game, \"deals damage\" means \"outputs a packet of damage and then other things can happen to it,\" and \"is dealt damage\" means \"HP are reduced.\" It's kind of confusing to have such similar-sounding names for these two different things, but at least it's self-consistent.</p>",
        "post_number": 21,
        "post_type": 1,
        "updated_at": "2021-02-07T02:13:23.126Z",
