      {
        "id": 39653,
        "name": "arenson9",
        "username": "arenson9",
        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/arenson9/{size}/1900_2.png",
        "created_at": "2012-10-04T21:23:35.000Z",
        "cooked": "<aside class=\"quote group-playtesters\" data-username=\"Spiff\">\n<div class=\"title\">\n<div class=\"quote-controls\"></div>\n<img loading=\"lazy\" alt=\"\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/spiff/48/1865_2.png\" class=\"avatar\"> Spiff:</div>\n<blockquote>\n<blockquote>\nI think Arenson9 commented that the requirement is that she deals herself damage, not that she is dealt damage.\n</blockquote>\nThat goes against the previous ruling by Christopher (I think) that if no damage is taken, then none has been dealt.\n</blockquote>\n</aside>\n<p>Sigh. I wish I had the time to go through all of the old threads in detail.</p>\n<p>There is ambiguity in what 'to deal' means. It might mean initiating an attack. It might mean the target actually taking damage. Perhaps <em>this</em> will be the thread where we marshall all of the known cases where something is triggered based on dealing/taking damage and we can then ask for a definitive ruling …</p>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<p>… but I don't have my cards in front of me at the moment.</p>",
